# Feature completeness (role / type / money)

When adding or changing a **CMS role**, **project type**, or **finance money/GST entity**, finish the full surface — do not stop at the happy path you touched.

## New or changed CMS role

Update **all** of these (or document why N/A):

1. `backend/src/constants/user-roles.js` — every relevant list (`userRoles`, staff, HRM, monitorable, etc.)
2. `frontend/src/lib/user-roles.ts` — mirror the same lists + labels/colors
3. `backend/openapi.yaml` + regenerate Zod (`api-zod`) role enums
4. Permission template in `permissions.service.js` (`cmsRole` must match)
5. Login home / nav / `PageOutlet` / `route-permissions` / `navigation.ts`
6. Team create/edit UI if the role is hireable (`fixedRole` or role picker)
7. Access scoping (projects, discussions, clients) for that role
8. Unit tests: extend `profile-page-roles` / `role-matrix-completeness` — **never leave expected arrays missing the new role**

## New or changed project type (e.g. digital)

1. Backend create/list filters and access rules
2. Admin create/edit form: **type-dependent fields** (labels + options) must switch with type; clear incompatible values on type change
3. Dedicated portal detail route must support team assign if membership scopes access
4. List/detail copy (“Tech stack” vs “Platforms”) must match type
5. Auto-provision side effects (e.g. digital workspace account)

## Finance / GST / ledgers

1. **One source of truth for GST** — do not count the same tax on two entities (e.g. expense `gstAmount` + vendor invoice). Prefer: bill holds GST; payment is cash only and links to the bill.
2. Wire Tax summary aggregations when adding a new GST-bearing document
3. Soft-delete / cancelled rows must be excluded from tax totals
4. Add unit tests for amount math and for “what feeds gstPaid / gstCollected”

## QA mindset before done

- [ ] New role/type appears in enums, permissions, nav, and tests
- [ ] Opposite portal (admin vs marketing vs finance) can complete the job end-to-end
- [ ] No duplicate money/GST paths without an explicit link field
- [ ] Regression tests updated in the same PR (stale expected arrays are bugs)
